# SQL's `LEFT JOIN` written as an operator: DS0105 with a fix to `join kind = leftouter`.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | LEFT JOIN 'customers.csv' on customerId
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..60
  PIPELINE@0..59
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    ERROR@20..59
      IDENT@20..24 "LEFT"
      WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
      IDENT@25..29 "JOIN"
      WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
      STRING@30..45 "'customers.csv'"
      WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
      IDENT@46..48 "on"
      WHITESPACE@48..49 " "
      IDENT@49..59 "customerId"
  WHITESPACE@59..60 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `LEFT JOIN` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:21
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | LEFT JOIN 'customers.csv' on customerId
  |                     ^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: the join kind goes after `join`: `join kind = leftouter`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | join kind = leftouter 'customers.csv' on customerId
which parses without errors
